 "capsule": "Cao (曹) was a small Zhou dynasty vassal state centered on Taoqiu in western Shandong near modern Dingtao, enfeoffed for Shu Zhenduo, a younger brother of King Wu of Zhou. A minor participant in Spring and Autumn diplomacy, frequently caught between larger neighbors such as Jin, Song, and Qi, Cao never became a major power in its own right. It was annexed by the state of Song in 487 BCE after the capture of its last ruler, Duke Fei, ending roughly five centuries of independent existence.",
